how gender-based discrimination had become deeply lodged in the belief system
of judges and others notwithstanding an impressive body of literature reporting
on empirical studies that show that deliberately false reports of sex abuse aimed
at an ex-partner by a vengeful woman are exceedingly rare: <q>The courts adopted
flawed practices at a time when no research was available and have continued
these discredited practices despite the current scientific research that rejects
them.</q> M.T. Hannah and B. Goldstein, eds., Domestic Violence, Abuse, and Child
Custody: Legal Strategies and Policy Issues, vol. II, xxviii.</p.1>
